1426
01:30:26,980 --> 01:30:30,520
Yeah, but what happens if they destroy it?

1427
01:30:30,600 --> 01:30:31,660
That is a possibility.

1428
01:30:32,100 --> 01:30:34,320
But, Hamamoto, I need you to trust me.

1429
01:30:34,500 --> 01:30:35,240
It'll be all right.

1430
01:30:36,160 --> 01:30:39,120
Aoyama, I'm coming along with you.

1431
01:30:39,540 --> 01:30:39,900
Uchida!

1432
01:30:39,900 --> 01:30:41,020
Hey, you!

1433
01:30:41,020 --> 01:30:45,720
What do you want now?

1434
01:30:46,520 --> 01:30:48,440
If you guys really want to get out of here,

1435
01:30:48,660 --> 01:30:49,400
we'll help you.

1436
01:30:49,780 --> 01:30:50,180
Huh?

1437
01:30:50,420 --> 01:30:54,200
So then, will you finally forgive me, Hamamoto?

1438
01:30:55,380 --> 01:30:56,780
I don't know if I can.

1439
01:30:58,860 --> 01:30:59,800
Hey, thanks.

1440
01:30:59,960 --> 01:31:00,780
We need your help.

1441
01:31:00,780 --> 01:31:04,680
There's a secret way.

1442
01:31:04,920 --> 01:31:05,320
Come on.

1443
01:31:15,320 --> 01:31:15,940
Hey, you okay?

1444
01:31:16,480 --> 01:31:17,400
Get back inside!

1445
01:31:17,780 --> 01:31:18,700
Crap, hurry!

1446
01:31:19,040 --> 01:31:19,580
Hamamoto!

1447
01:31:19,580 --> 01:31:24,360
You okay?

1448
01:31:24,700 --> 01:31:25,940
No, dang it!

1449
01:31:27,720 --> 01:31:28,520
This way!

1450
01:31:33,080 --> 01:31:33,640
Hey!

1451
01:31:33,760 --> 01:31:34,660
What is that?

1452
01:31:35,240 --> 01:31:36,340
It's huge!

1453
01:31:37,740 --> 01:31:38,620
The ocean!

1454
01:31:38,620 --> 01:31:40,580
Wait, so that's the floating ball

1455
01:31:40,580 --> 01:31:42,080
you guys were doing the research on?

1456
01:31:42,420 --> 01:31:43,960
Hey, what are you doing?

1457
01:31:44,200 --> 01:31:45,260
We're evacuating!

1458
01:31:45,260 --> 01:31:47,040
You guys run!

1459
01:31:47,180 --> 01:31:48,000
I got this!

1460
01:31:55,180 --> 01:31:56,000
Hey, come back!

1461
01:31:56,420 --> 01:31:56,840
Come on!

1462
01:31:57,240 --> 01:31:58,140
Let go!

1463
01:31:58,400 --> 01:31:59,020
Let go!

1464
01:32:01,160 --> 01:32:01,540
Stop it!

1465
01:32:01,540 --> 01:32:01,880
Let go!

1466
01:32:01,880 --> 01:32:02,840
Dirty, old man!

1467
01:32:10,220 --> 01:32:11,720
Get moving, Aoyama!

1468
01:32:15,260 --> 01:32:45,240
It seems you've solved the mess.

1469
01:32:45,240 --> 01:32:45,480
It's a mystery.

1470
01:32:46,300 --> 01:32:46,640
Yeah.

1471
01:32:49,360 --> 01:32:51,800
Just like the penguins aren't real penguins,

1472
01:32:52,600 --> 01:32:54,820
well, you aren't human.

1473
01:32:57,200 --> 01:33:00,740
You, the penguins, and the ocean were all linked.

1474
01:33:01,620 --> 01:33:04,640
Some kind of energy was being emitted from the ocean.

1475
01:33:05,540 --> 01:33:08,640
It seems to have been fueling both you and the penguins.

1476
01:33:10,360 --> 01:33:11,900
The penguin energy.

1477
01:33:11,900 --> 01:33:12,900
Correct.

1478
01:33:12,900 --> 01:33:12,920
Correct.

1479
01:33:13,380 --> 01:33:16,700
I realized that the penguins' ability to destroy the ocean

1480
01:33:16,700 --> 01:33:18,560
was an extremely important detail.

1481
01:33:20,340 --> 01:33:21,820
Quick, we need to hide.

1482
01:33:21,820 --> 01:33:39,660
So, young man, what is the ocean, then?

1483
01:33:39,660 --> 01:33:44,320
The ocean, it warps both space and time.

1484
01:33:44,920 --> 01:33:49,180
That's why I hypothesize that it should not exist in this world.

1485
01:33:49,180 --> 01:33:55,420
And if that's true, and the ocean isn't a physical object,

1486
01:33:55,420 --> 01:33:57,620
if it's a hole...

1487
01:33:57,620 --> 01:33:59,060
A hole?

1488
01:33:59,700 --> 01:34:00,800
A rip in the world.

1489
01:34:01,200 --> 01:34:04,540
Or maybe it's the edge of the world that's somehow hidden itself

1490
01:34:04,540 --> 01:34:06,580
in the interior of the world.

1491
01:34:06,920 --> 01:34:07,640
You lost me.

1492
01:34:07,640 --> 01:34:10,260
The penguins weren't destroying the ocean.

1493
01:34:10,680 --> 01:34:12,140
They were repairing the world.

1494
01:34:13,220 --> 01:34:17,120
So then, I create the penguins in order to plug the hole in the world?

1495
01:34:17,460 --> 01:34:19,700
It's just a guess, but it could explain everything.

1496
01:34:21,280 --> 01:34:22,260
Great work.

1497
01:34:22,800 --> 01:34:24,020
Nothing here. Let's go.

1498
01:34:24,540 --> 01:34:25,180
Yes, sir!

1499
01:34:25,180 --> 01:34:28,940
